WEBVTT

01:06.820 --> 01:07.760
Where's Malik?

01:09.710 --> 01:12.010
Stuck in bed with a cold, I'm afraid.

01:14.400 --> 01:17.100
The bug going around 
this year is a nasty one.

01:17.100 --> 01:18.770
Just awful, isn't it?

01:20.790 --> 01:22.640
Mind if I take a look at what's inside?

02:11.600 --> 02:13.300
Rouge, would you mind?

02:18.800 --> 02:20.460
There.

02:34.900 --> 02:36.550
Who's got a cold, now?

02:37.290 --> 02:40.030
That's Malik lying over there, isn't it?

02:42.710 --> 02:43.710
Malik...

02:44.130 --> 02:46.190
Oh, Malik!

02:46.190 --> 02:49.600
How could you have died of a simple cold?!

02:49.600 --> 02:51.120
Enough bullshit!

02:51.120 --> 02:53.440
Come, now. I'm being quite serious.

02:53.800 --> 02:55.450
Just who are you?

03:05.730 --> 03:07.540
Who... am...

03:08.510 --> 03:09.290
I?

03:11.340 --> 03:12.350
Rouge.

03:12.760 --> 03:13.930
Rouge.

03:15.110 --> 03:16.920
Take care of this, would you?

03:16.920 --> 03:18.660
Oh, sure.

03:23.140 --> 03:24.200
Outta the way.

03:24.200 --> 03:25.700
Sorry...

03:25.700 --> 03:28.690
I'm so sorry. She's new at this.

03:29.070 --> 03:31.920
Come on, Rouge. No spacing out.

03:40.610 --> 03:43.390
There's Sarah's bad habit again.

03:43.390 --> 03:45.910
Was it really smart to 
take in a girl like that?

03:46.230 --> 03:47.370
Huh?

03:47.740 --> 03:49.910
Er...

03:50.980 --> 03:51.960
Here you go.

03:51.960 --> 03:54.380
Oh, thank you.

03:54.380 --> 03:57.480
Yo, Scar Head! Get this place 
cleaned up already!

03:57.950 --> 03:59.890
Don't think you can slack off 
'cause you're a Nean!

03:59.890 --> 04:01.210
I'm sorry.

04:03.650 --> 04:06.520
See you tomorrow. Have a good night, Rouge.

04:06.520 --> 04:08.810
Same to you, Ms. Sarah.

04:15.620 --> 04:17.300
It's gone?

04:17.300 --> 04:19.190
I know it was here this morning.

04:19.190 --> 04:20.800
Here, use mine.

04:22.310 --> 04:25.910
I can't. Then you'll cease to function.

04:25.910 --> 04:27.710
And if that happens, you'll be discarded.

04:34.540 --> 04:36.510
See ya later, rookie.

04:37.550 --> 04:40.440
But you need your shot of Nectar 
before the day ends, too.

04:40.440 --> 04:42.590
Don't worry. I'm sure it's here somewhere.

04:43.230 --> 04:44.250
Yeah...

04:47.660 --> 04:49.190
Long day, eh?

04:49.190 --> 04:51.190
Who's entertaining our star tonight?

04:51.190 --> 04:53.180
Some hotshot from Panacea.

04:53.180 --> 04:55.210
Talk about your ideal patron.

04:55.210 --> 04:56.860
Here's to Sarah Fitzgerald,

04:56.860 --> 05:01.000
the diva of Club Canal who's 
keeping food on all our tables.

05:01.000 --> 05:02.490
Where's Kevin, anyway?

05:05.600 --> 05:07.490
Something good happen to him or what?

05:07.490 --> 05:08.330
Check it out!

05:09.640 --> 05:12.170
Nectar sells for a fortune.

05:12.170 --> 05:16.820
And when a human uses it, they get a 
taste of Heaven on Earth, apparently.

05:17.410 --> 05:19.880
It's on you if that comes back to bite you.

05:19.880 --> 05:22.880
They've all got the Asimov 
Code programmed into 'em.

05:22.880 --> 05:25.430
They can't defy us humans.

05:25.690 --> 05:29.670
Yo, did you know Neans are alien spies?

05:29.670 --> 05:32.960
What, like, Visitors? 
You actually believe that?

05:37.070 --> 05:38.940
<i>So what did you think, tweet?</i>

05:38.940 --> 05:41.680
I don't think it's her.

05:41.680 --> 05:43.480
<i>State your reasoning.</i>

05:45.340 --> 05:49.600
Well... It's just a hunch, really...

05:49.600 --> 05:51.220
<i>Then it contributes nothing.</i>

05:51.220 --> 05:52.730
<i>Who was that man with her?</i>

05:52.730 --> 05:55.810
An executive from Panacea. 
I think his name's... Herman...

05:55.810 --> 05:57.120
<i>Herman Heyward?</i>

05:57.120 --> 05:58.280
That's it!

05:58.280 --> 06:00.490
I looked really closely, but...

06:01.380 --> 06:04.640
I couldn't see a Nectar intake unit on him.

06:04.640 --> 06:07.550
<i>Just looking won't tell you anything! 
That's true for you, isn't it?</i>

06:07.550 --> 06:08.870
I guess so.

06:08.870 --> 06:10.280
<i>Tweet! Tweet!</i>

06:10.280 --> 06:14.050
<i>You need to stick closer to Sarah 
and get conclusive proof!</i>

06:14.050 --> 06:16.440
<i>Action comes after that, tweet!</i>

06:23.540 --> 06:27.130
<i>Tweet. I'll be waiting behind 
the theater at noon. Tweet.</i>

06:27.130 --> 06:27.990
For what?

06:27.990 --> 06:29.160
<i>Your regular report.</i>

06:29.160 --> 06:30.560
Oh...

06:30.560 --> 06:31.940
<i>Self-awareness intact?</i>

06:31.940 --> 06:32.910
I think so.

06:35.650 --> 06:36.830
Roger!

06:55.060 --> 06:56.660
What is it?

07:31.230 --> 07:32.460
Are you all right?!

07:44.480 --> 07:46.570
A red Gladiator...

07:48.610 --> 07:50.830
Sarah! Are you hurt?

08:02.460 --> 08:04.420
Ow!

08:14.520 --> 08:15.960
Are you all right?

08:16.480 --> 08:19.160
<i>This is footage taken 
by an anonymous citizen</i>

08:19.160 --> 08:22.270
<i>of the scene of the murder 
that took place in the suburbs.</i>

08:23.530 --> 08:27.000
<i>The video seems to become 
distorted in the vicinity</i>

08:27.000 --> 08:29.290
<i>of this individual who 
seems to be the suspect.</i>

08:29.290 --> 08:33.200
<i>There must be some sort 
of interference in the—</i>

08:30.600 --> 08:32.590
What a pain.

08:33.200 --> 08:35.670
Yeah. It's probably the same one.

08:35.670 --> 08:37.020
That's right.

08:37.580 --> 08:40.210
Yeah, he showed up here, too.

08:45.760 --> 08:47.770
The sender didn't give a name.

08:47.770 --> 08:49.030
I see.

08:57.210 --> 08:58.500
Give it back...

08:58.500 --> 09:01.520
Please... give me back... my Nectar!

09:01.850 --> 09:05.010
What're you on? I dunno 
what you're talkin' about.

09:06.480 --> 09:08.840
Please... Please!

09:35.120 --> 09:36.610
Well, that's reality.

09:38.170 --> 09:39.610
Hey, I'm here.

09:39.610 --> 09:42.490
Um... Who were you again?

09:43.990 --> 09:45.270
Tweet, tweet.

09:45.740 --> 09:48.280
Oh! The bird's voice!

09:54.440 --> 09:57.510
I had no idea there was an actual 
person talking through that bird.

09:57.510 --> 09:58.400
Hmm?

09:58.860 --> 10:03.950
Oh... I said, I had no idea there was an 
actual person talking through that bird.

10:04.440 --> 10:05.420
Hmm?

10:07.610 --> 10:10.140
I said, I had no idea there was—

10:10.140 --> 10:12.500
What, is your memory broken?!

10:13.200 --> 10:15.930
So... who are you, exactly?

10:16.300 --> 10:19.170
I'm Naomi Orthmann. Nice to meet you.

10:19.170 --> 10:21.430
I've been supporting you.

10:21.740 --> 10:24.700
Well, that's kind of you. Um, I'm—

10:24.700 --> 10:25.660
I know you.

10:25.660 --> 10:27.060
Well, thank you.

10:30.070 --> 10:31.530
Excuse me!

10:31.530 --> 10:36.020
An extra-large fried rice, twice-cooked pork,
mapo tofu, and two jajangmyeon!

10:36.020 --> 10:39.580
So, um, where's the bird?

10:39.580 --> 10:41.070
It died.

10:41.070 --> 10:42.580
Oh, what a shame.

10:42.580 --> 10:44.180
My condolences.

10:44.180 --> 10:45.830
Thank you kindly.

10:49.330 --> 10:51.420
So, any progress since then?

10:51.920 --> 10:56.490
No. I still don't think Sarah is Viola.

10:56.490 --> 10:59.170
Yeah, it's not her.

11:01.630 --> 11:03.710
Sorry to tell you this,

11:03.710 --> 11:06.400
but Sarah Fitzgerald was 
injecting herself with Nectar.

11:08.470 --> 11:12.880
She's a Nean, and most likely, 
one of the Immortal Nine.

11:12.880 --> 11:15.570
Viola Keane, also known as...

11:16.000 --> 11:18.670
...Purgatory Viola.

11:23.640 --> 11:26.430
Confess your sins.

11:26.430 --> 11:27.500
Stop that.

11:27.500 --> 11:29.910
I would've preferred never to see you again.

11:29.910 --> 11:31.500
Now, that's just cold.

11:31.500 --> 11:33.760
I need you to keep your promise.

11:33.760 --> 11:37.760
Of course I will. However, 
I ran into a little trouble.

11:37.760 --> 11:40.280
I gave you all the information you needed.

11:40.280 --> 11:41.850
Yes, you did!

11:41.850 --> 11:46.020
Oh, you went so far as to 
taint your own body—no,

11:46.020 --> 11:50.120
you put your body on the line 
to get me that information!

11:50.120 --> 11:54.150
And all the Nectar was taken right out 
from under me. What a massive failure.

11:54.760 --> 11:58.510
Well, I'm sorry to hear that, 
but it's not my concern.

11:58.510 --> 12:01.280
It was the red guy who took it.

12:01.980 --> 12:06.910
Yes! The archenemy of us Alters, 
the one who killed Nius and Achillus!

12:06.910 --> 12:10.000
The very same red Gladiator!

12:10.000 --> 12:11.700
He came after me, too.

12:11.700 --> 12:13.820
What?! Thank goodness you're safe!

12:13.820 --> 12:15.170
Keep your promise!

12:16.520 --> 12:18.780
You have my sympathy.

12:18.780 --> 12:20.900
If this job had been a success,

12:20.900 --> 12:24.040
you could have cut ties with us Alters.

12:24.780 --> 12:26.930
But that was only a fleeting dream.

12:27.240 --> 12:28.590
Giallon...

12:28.590 --> 12:33.260
One of our own, Silvia, suspects 
that you leaked that information.

12:33.260 --> 12:34.440
She does?

12:34.440 --> 12:38.900
I insisted that you were innocent, but...

12:38.900 --> 12:41.250
I was nearly killed!

12:41.250 --> 12:42.620
That's just the thing.

12:42.940 --> 12:46.530
I want to protect you, even if it 
means defying the organization.

12:47.110 --> 12:49.000
Has anything odd happened lately?

12:49.870 --> 12:52.810
Anyone unfamiliar tried to approach you?

13:10.700 --> 13:14.240
He who makes the first move wins.

13:16.390 --> 13:18.430
Aren't you gonna eat?

13:18.430 --> 13:19.800
This is enough.

13:26.650 --> 13:27.410
Huh?

13:28.670 --> 13:31.790
What?! What, what, what?!

13:33.580 --> 13:37.820
<i>This is the footage of the suspect 
at the scene of last night's murder</i>

13:37.820 --> 13:40.550
<i>with as much of the static 
removed as possible.</i>

13:42.160 --> 13:43.330
Who's that?

13:43.330 --> 13:45.110
Can't you tell?

13:46.420 --> 13:48.040
I don't recognize him.

13:48.040 --> 13:49.100
That's okay.

13:49.100 --> 13:50.730
I've got a pretty good idea.

13:50.730 --> 13:54.000
<i>It has been pointed out that 
the suspect closely resembles</i>

13:54.000 --> 13:58.090
<i>the suspect spotted at the 
murder of Dr. Roy Junghardt,</i>

13:58.090 --> 14:00.840
<i>a researcher at a well-known 
Nean research lab.</i>

14:00.840 --> 14:03.830
Come on, eat some meat.

14:03.830 --> 14:05.010
I prefer this.

14:14.270 --> 14:15.140
Um...

14:15.140 --> 14:17.740
Would you mind accompanying me tonight?

14:20.360 --> 14:23.470
I crossed this bridge to come here.

14:23.910 --> 14:28.270
I abandoned my real self from the past 
on the other side of this bridge,

14:28.270 --> 14:30.900
hoping to become a brand-new me.

14:33.760 --> 14:37.080
What is one's "real self," I wonder?

14:42.310 --> 14:43.950
Viola Keane.

14:45.370 --> 14:48.510
I liked you. I really did.

14:50.230 --> 14:52.000
Neans can't kill people.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.240
We're not your standard Neans.

14:55.980 --> 14:59.000
You're the same as us, aren't you?

15:24.360 --> 15:25.680
Oops.

15:25.680 --> 15:27.320
Was that the wrong one?

15:27.320 --> 15:29.510
You're... Giallon?!

15:29.510 --> 15:34.710
Well, silly me. 
I was certain she was the one.

15:35.120 --> 15:38.220
I forgot about your ability to mimic.

15:38.220 --> 15:40.590
So the one who attacked me then...

15:40.590 --> 15:43.130
Yep! It was me!

15:44.500 --> 15:46.260
Hell Giallon...

15:46.260 --> 15:49.430
That's him? Whew, scary.

15:49.840 --> 15:51.640
Why did you attack me?

15:51.640 --> 15:54.460
Why, out of the kindness of my heart!

15:54.460 --> 15:56.870
I just thought I'd give you a little push.

15:56.870 --> 15:59.900
You know I would never kill you!

15:59.900 --> 16:01.680
I just stopped right before!

16:01.680 --> 16:05.460
Oh, I'm such a kind man!

16:05.460 --> 16:07.340
I mean, you were hesitating!

16:07.340 --> 16:10.320
Couldn't you have killed that cutie yourself?

16:10.830 --> 16:12.030
I could have.

16:12.030 --> 16:15.030
I had my doubts. 
That's why I stepped up to—

16:15.030 --> 16:17.040
Rouge wasn't the red Gladiator!

16:17.040 --> 16:18.890
She had nothing to do with this!

16:18.890 --> 16:22.550
Are you sure about that? She knew your name,

16:22.550 --> 16:23.550
Viola.

16:24.060 --> 16:28.390
Well, she was probably an agent of Aletheia. 
Just one of their dogs.

16:28.390 --> 16:31.770
Killing her was just the right thing to do!

16:40.050 --> 16:42.850
Well, I certainly didn't expect this!

16:57.320 --> 17:00.330
Gosh, this sure is fun!

17:00.330 --> 17:02.400
But this is as far as I go.

17:02.400 --> 17:05.000
You said earlier that you 
could've killed her.

17:05.000 --> 17:07.110
From now on, you're the star...

17:07.110 --> 17:09.510
and it's showtime!

17:09.510 --> 17:14.800
Take her out and keep on singing 
to your heart's content!

17:14.800 --> 17:17.490
And with that, adieu, Viola!

17:28.460 --> 17:31.360
Before I kill you, tell me your name.

17:31.850 --> 17:33.870
Metal Rouge.

17:47.400 --> 17:50.520
I am one of the Immortal Nine,

17:50.520 --> 17:52.680
Purgatory Viola!

18:01.340 --> 18:02.610
Not bad.

18:24.380 --> 18:25.290
<i>Don't evade her!</i>

18:25.580 --> 18:26.290
Naomi?

18:26.290 --> 18:29.000
If you take just a few more hits, 
I can analyze her!

18:39.770 --> 18:42.770
Why did you kill Nius and Achillus?

18:42.770 --> 18:44.520
Why are you after us?

18:45.260 --> 18:47.150
Just who are you?!

18:51.660 --> 18:54.370
She's using ion acceleration 
on part of her arm.

18:54.370 --> 18:56.870
And they're equipped with 
high-frequency blades, too?

19:01.000 --> 19:04.100
All I wanted to do was sing!

19:04.870 --> 19:07.350
I only wanted to be happy!

19:09.290 --> 19:12.550
Why is that so wrong?!

19:12.550 --> 19:13.880
Are you done, Naomi?!

19:13.880 --> 19:14.880
<i>Just sent it off!</i>

19:26.460 --> 19:27.850
Cheeky brat!

19:29.600 --> 19:30.570
Tell me!

19:30.570 --> 19:33.820
How are we different from humans?!

19:45.770 --> 19:48.380
I will live! I won't die!

19:50.050 --> 19:53.880
Your pressure resistance is at breaking point!
Your outer shell's gonna melt!

19:54.360 --> 19:57.970
This ends now!

20:32.550 --> 20:36.360
It was raining like this 
the day we first met, too.

21:09.930 --> 21:11.300
Where to next?

21:12.420 --> 21:14.370
That's already been decided.
